        "original_id": "6d4849e9-c4be-5663-93bc-ec70b9906f36",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mel Shaw, Roger Allers, Rob Minkoff, Don Hahn, Irene Mecchi, Jonathan Roberts, Linda Woolverton\n- Films: The Rescuers, The Fox and the Hound, The Black Cauldron, The Great Mouse Detective, Beauty and the Beast, The Lion King\n- Roles: animation design, story, directors, producer, screenwriters\n\nFacts:\n- In 1977, Mel Shaw had an animated film credit on The Rescuers, usually involving animation design or story work.\n- In 1981, Mel Shaw had an animated film credit on The Fox and the Hound, usually involving animation design or story work.\n- In 1985, Mel Shaw had an animated film credit on The Black Cauldron, usually involving animation design or story work.\n- In 1986, Mel Shaw had an animated film credit on The Great Mouse Detective, usually involving animation design or story work.\n- In 1991, Mel Shaw had an animated film credit on Beauty and the Beast, usually involving animation design or story work.\n- In 1994, Mel Shaw had an animated film credit on The Lion King, usually involving animation design or story work.\n- The Lion King was directed by Roger Allers and Rob Minkoff.\n- The Lion King was produced by Don Hahn.\n- The Lion King screenplay was credited to Irene Mecchi, Jonathan Roberts, and Linda Woolverton.",
